  "title": "design-map-has-no-read-edit-toggle-and-saves-first-drag",
  "requirement": "AC-7 / FR3 / REQ-253: the panel has no read/edit toggle; after opening the page the first drag on a node is saved to the page file and survives a reload. This case verifies the no-toggle/always-edit source contract and the save-to-file round trip the panel uses; the real pointer drag is the implementer's browser proof, not re-driven here.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "tests/designmap-instruments/panel-surface.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node tests/designmap-instruments/panel-surface.mjs --case AC-7",
  "steps": [
    "Read client/page-view.jsx, client/host.js and src/command.mjs from the tree under test; assert no read/edit toggle and that saves are element-driven and debounced.",
    "Create a page and a node through the map tools, read the scene through the /designmap command, move the node as a drag would, save through op save.",
    "Read the page file and reopen the page through the command; the moved coordinates must be there."
  ],
  "expected": "The page editor renders no read/edit toggle and never branches on a read or edit mode; a canvas change is debounced from the elements and saved through host.savePage with command op save; the command re-reads and writes the scene to the same page file, and a reload reads the moved node back.",
